# Web3Forms access key for the service request form. OPTIONAL.
#
# The form has two delivery paths and chooses automatically:
#
#   key set        → Web3Forms. Relays to the destination inbox. Works on any
#                    host. Takes precedence when present.
#   no key, on Netlify
#                  → Netlify Forms. Submissions land in the Netlify dashboard.
#                    Works with no configuration, because scripts/postbuild.mjs
#                    writes the form-detection markup Netlify needs.
#                    You MUST set a notification email under
#                    Netlify → Forms → Settings, or nobody is told.
#   no key, localhost
#                  → Preview. The form validates fully, delivers nothing, and
#                    says so plainly on the confirmation screen. It never
#                    reports a success that did not happen.
#
# Every build prints which path it produced. See GOING-LIVE.md section 2.
#
# Get a key free at https://web3forms.com — it is tied to the destination
# inbox and is safe to expose in client-side code. It must be present at BUILD
# time (Vite inlines it), so set it in Netlify's environment variables too.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
